2. Eligible internal use

Subject to every condition in this license, Licensor grants you a worldwide,
nonexclusive, royalty-free copyright license to copy, run, inspect, and modify
the Software solely for the internal operations of a Qualifying Company for
which you work. Employees and contractors may exercise these permissions on
that company's behalf and under these same conditions.

A "Qualifying Company" has both:
(a) fewer than 100 employees and independent contractors in total; and
(b) total revenue in its previous tax year below US$1,000,000 measured in 2019
dollars, adjusted for inflation using the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics
CPI-U, U.S. city average, all items, not seasonally adjusted, base 1982-1984=100.

For these tests, a company includes the business or organization for which you
work and every entity that controls it, is controlled by it, or is under common
control with it. Control means ownership of substantially all assets or power
to direct management and policies, directly or indirectly.

Internal operations may include using the Software to produce work products
for customers. That permission does not extend to giving customers or other
third parties access to the Software's functionality as described in section 3.
Use by or for a company that does not meet both thresholds requires a separate
written commercial license from Licensor.

3. Hosted and managed services

Without a separate written commercial license from Licensor, you may not use,
copy, modify, distribute, or make the Software available to provide third
parties a hosted or managed service that gives them access to a substantial
part of the Software's memory storage, retrieval, search, knowledge-management,
or agent-memory functionality.

This restriction applies whether the service is paid or free, whether the
Software is modified or unmodified, and whether access is supplied through a
user interface, API, integration, reseller, or white-label offering. Rebranding,
wrapping, or combining the Software with other software does not remove this
restriction. A Qualifying Company is also subject to this restriction.

Employees and contractors accessing a deployment solely for the eligible
company's own internal operations are not third-party service customers for
this section. A contractor's assistance installing or maintaining that
deployment does not authorize the contractor to offer the Software's
functionality to customers as its own hosted or managed service.

This license does not restrict independently developed software that does not
use or incorporate the Software, and does not grant exclusive rights in ideas,
protocols, or functionality as such.

